@@ -1,5 +1,47 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased — integer profile revision 2: promotion, sharing, chunked storage
+
+- Mixed-representation algebra no longer degrades to sorted codes. One operand is
+  promoted into the other's representation (`from_lsb0_bytes` for dense windows,
+  bulk append for sorted codes) or a copy of the larger operand is edited; the
+  direction follows a documented work estimate. Dense unions beyond the window
+  limit become Roaring instead of a sorted array of every member.
+- Storage is reference counted: `Clone` is O(1), and a result equal to one of its
+  operands shares that operand's allocation (`shares_storage_with`). Equality,
+  ordering and hashing compare same representations natively and hash every
+  representation through identical code chunks.
+- Add explicit chunked storage (`IntSetPolicy::chunked`, `IntSetRepr::Chunked`):
+  2^16-code `Array`/`Bitmap`/`Full` containers behind `Arc`, shared between
+  results and operands and combined without reading when physically identical
+  (`shared_chunks`, `chunk_count`). The automatic planner does not select it.
+- Sets carry their construction limits (`policy()`); results inherit the larger
+  limit of their operands, so dense budgets bound algebra results in both
+  directions.
+- Planner: dense windows of at most 4 KiB within budget are always chosen;
+  Roaring candidates are built with bulk appends and range inserts for runs of
+  32 or more, then run-optimized.
+- Dense kernels run over three slice regions with the result count fused into
+  the pass.
+- `IntKey` for `u8`, `u16`, `i8`, `i16`, `char`, `usize`, `isize`, `NonZeroU8`,
+  `NonZeroU16`, with checked decoding of foreign codes.
+- `int-set` needs only `alloc`: `roaring` is pulled without default features and
+  `std` forwards `roaring/std` (runtime SIMD dispatch). The `roaring-0_12` backend
+  feature still implies `std`. The integer profile builds for
+  `thumbv7em-none-eabihf`. The downstream key fixture's lockfile shrank
+  accordingly.
+- Benchmark `integer_sets` adds the chunked policy, mixed union/difference
+  materialization, snapshot-style updates, clone and equality cases, and now
+  requires `int-set,roaring-0_12`. Measurements, a same-binary A/B harness and
+  the review probes are recorded under `verification/int-set/revision2/`; see
+  `docs/integer-benchmarks.md` (revision 2), `docs/reviews/integer-profile-adversarial-review.md`,
+  and `docs/design/proposals/integer-collections.md`.
+- Documented trade-off: a dense set that gains far-away members grows its window
+  (within twice the sorted payload) rather than becoming sorted; such updates
+  measured 0.76× on one fixture while every other representation's snapshot
+  updates sped up 3–625×. Scattered `u64` data stays sorted; chunked storage is
+  the slowest candidate there and is explicit only.
+
 ## Unreleased — typed integer profile
 
 - Add the explicit `integer::FrozenIntSet<K>` profile and complete `int-set`
