+## Integer profile revision 2: eager algebra with shared, promoted results
+
+Decision: set algebra on `FrozenIntSet` stays eager and value-returning. What
+changed is what it materializes and how results relate to operands.
+
+- **Promotion over degradation.** A mixed pair promotes one operand into the
+  other's representation, or edits a copy of the larger operand, chosen by a
+  work estimate in word units. The alternative — lazy views as the result type —
+  was explored and researched: no production system answers `contains` on an
+  unmaterialized expression as a primary operation, chained lazy unions make the
+  snapshot pattern O(N) per probe, and element-wise seeking through the Roaring
+  iterator measured slower than probing. Views remain a future explicit,
+  borrowed API (see the proposal).
+- **Sharing as the fix for versioned workloads.** `Arc` storage with identity
+  sharing at the whole-set level, and chunked storage with per-container sharing
+  and physical-identity shortcuts (`A ∪ A = A`, `A ∖ A = ∅`). Rejected: making
+  chunked storage the automatic default — its per-container overhead is paid per
+  member on scattered codes, where sorted storage is right; rejected: hidden
+  materialization caches, which would make a membership test allocate.
+- **Budgets travel with sets.** A limit chosen at construction is part of the
+  set's contract for its results; results inherit the larger operand limit so a
+  small budget is honored and a large one is not clamped.
+- **Measurement of record.** Before/after claims come from one executable that
+  links both versions of the profile and alternates measurements; two benchmark
+  binaries moved unchanged control loops by up to 2× on the review host.
+- **Deferred:** streaming constructors, a frozen single-allocation chunk arena,
+  borrowed expression views, rank-indexed maps, range sets and the other items in
+  `proposals/integer-collections.md`.
