+### Shared storage
+
+Storage sits behind an `Arc`. `clone()` is O(1), and a materialized operation
+whose result equals one of its operands returns that operand's allocation:
+`a ∪ ∅`, `a ∩ a`, a union whose count equals the larger operand's, an
+intersection whose count equals the smaller's, a difference that removed
+nothing. `shares_storage_with` reports this for diagnostics. Equality,
+ordering and hashing check allocation identity first, then compare same
+representations natively (slice, window words, native Roaring, container
+pairs) and only fall back to the code stream for differing representations.
+Hashing feeds every representation the same 64-code chunks, so the hash is
+representation-independent for any hasher.
+
+Sets also carry the limits they were built with (`policy()`); results inherit
+the larger limit of their operands, so a dense budget chosen at construction
+bounds the dense windows that algebra may allocate.
+
 Counts are u64. Inclusive encoded spans are u128, because the inclusive span
